# Requirements — Statement review: every figure traced, the unclear lines first

Bet: statement-review, signed 2026-11-16. Scope is a showcase for one firm (D15, D24): a working model the underwriter can try, after which the firm's approver decides on a pilot (D14, D25). Forms and risk tags follow the template.

Revision 33, after D315 (changes requested on 2026-11-21, the owner's decision of 2026-11-20 given in chat, after T17's eleventh review, verify-197; the owner had answered revision 32's question as D309, and D310 approved revision 32). Only P5 changes; its id, form and risk tag do not. D309 kept revision 32's default: a supplied policy's own text stays within P5, and T17 keeps its mask. T17's tenth review, verify-195, then found a custom rule's limits reaching the prompt in its requirement and detail cells, which the owner's 97e4026 masks as well. verify-197, T17's eleventh review, judged 97e4026 and failed P5 because the prompt's period line writes the statement's first and last dates, and a description can hold the same date: with the first date 2026-09-30 and 2026-09-30 in a transaction description, every prompt holds the description's string, under the shipped policy as under a custom one. Revision 32's scope excepted the text the tool writes into every prompt, and said that a figure's value and a rule's outcome are not among it, since the case decides them. No build can keep the period's dates out of a prompt that R30 lets carry the period. D315 accepts this as an edge case outside the guarantee, to push development forward, and asks for one scope limit under P5, keeping everything else in revision 32. R30 lets every prompt carry the period and the metric and rule tables, whose values the case decides: the period's dates, each figure's value and each rule's outcome. A string of the case's descriptions or profile that coincides with one of those values as the prompt writes it is the case's figure, not line-level data, and is no sentinel for P5; otherwise P5 and R30 contradict each other, since a prompt must carry the period. P5 is about text reaching a prompt from a description or profile field, which stays a sentinel. P5's scope of revision 33 states it. Revision 33 makes four readings. First, the values the case decides are read wherever the prompt writes them